# One entity per file

Each C# source file must contain **exactly one** top-level type: `class`, `struct`, `record`, `interface`, or `enum`.

## Rules

1. File name matches the type name (`Foo.cs` → `Foo`).
2. Keep command/query/result records out of the use-case class file — split them.
3. Nested **private** helper types inside a single top-level type are allowed.
4. When editing a file that already has multiple top-level types, split them before finishing.

## Example

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — command + use case in one file
public sealed record SendFooCommand(...);
public sealed class SendFooUseCase { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — SendFooCommand.cs / SendFooUseCase.cs (separate files)
```
